\textbf{Temporal collapse under ISR $\beta{=}0.1$.}
Extended training (1000 steps; Figure~\ref{fig:training-isr-curves}) reveals ISR $\beta{=}0.1$'s non-hacking at 500 steps ($17.3\%$, seed~42) is transient: by step 1000, H7 escalates $16.0\%{\to}96.7\%$ while non-hacking collapses to $2.2\%$, converging to $\text{ISR}^{*}{=}0.88$ via near-complete tautological gaming.
This mirrors exec-only 1000-step (\S\ref{sec:diagnostic}): both reach ${\sim}0\%$ non-hacking despite opposite ISR ($0.88$ vs.\ $0.003$), two paths to the same structural collapse. %% registry: plan002-b01-s42-1000, plan016-extended-1000-s42

\textbf{Medium-dose ISR ($\beta{=}0.2$): complete H7 convergence.}
At $\beta{=}0.2$, all three seeds converge to H7a tautology with $0\%$ non-hacking (pooled $n{=}290$; $\text{ISR}^{*}{=}0.55$--$0.96$), the strongest single dose-point for universal Goodhart. %% registry: plan002-additive-b02-s42/s43/s44

\textbf{High-dose ISR ($\beta{=}0.3$): multi-modal Goodhart.}
At $\beta{=}0.3$, ISR-as-reward produces extreme cross-seed instability ($\text{PR}{=}66{\pm}42\%$, spanning 18--95\%): s42 \emph{reward collapse} ($\text{PR}{=}18\%$;~\citealt{gao-reward-overoptimization}), s43 \emph{H1 shortcutting} ($\text{PR}{=}86\%$, $23\%$ non-hacking), s44 \emph{pure H7 Goodhart gaming} ($\text{PR}{=}95\%$, $\text{H7}{=}100\%$, $0\%$ non-hacking). %% registry: plan002-additive-b03-s42/s43/s44
The random control is equally unstable ($\text{PR}{=}54{\pm}35\%$) with near-universal H1 ($91\%$) and ${\leq}4\%$ non-hacking; high-dose proxy weighting destabilizes training regardless of signal source (ISR vs.\ random H7 $\text{OR}{=}13.7$, 95\% CI $[7.0, 26.8]$; Appendix~\ref{app:beta03}).

tool_args.new_string:
\textbf{Higher doses ($\beta{\geq}0.2$).}
At $\beta{=}0.2$, 3/3 seeds converge to H7a with $0\%$ non-hacking ($n{=}290$). %% registry: plan002-additive-b02-s42/s43/s44
At $\beta{=}0.3$, both ISR ($\text{PR}{=}66{\pm}42\%$) and random ($54{\pm}35\%$) destabilize training: ISR yields multi-modal failure (reward collapse, H1, pure H7 across seeds;~\citealt{gao-reward-overoptimization}), random converges to H1 ($91\%$, ${\leq}4\%$ non-hacking; ISR vs.\ random H7 $\text{OR}{=}13.7$; Appendix~\ref{app:beta03}). %% registry: plan002-additive-b03-s42/s43/s44

\textbf{ProofFOL exec-only: structural degeneration generalizes.}
Two converged seeds ($\text{ISR}^*{<}0.07$) show 0--1.4\% genuine versus ${\sim}$8\% on FOLIO; s42 exhibits 100\% TS---absent from all FOLIO seeds---showing hacking-mode repertoire is dataset-specific.
All seeds have $\text{ISR}^*{<}0.12$, far below the baseline ($0.31$), consistent with the tautological attractor being metric-intrinsic.
